    "http://purl.bdrc.io/ontology/core/biblioNote" : [ { 
      "type" : "literal" ,
      "value" : "This print was made from newly carved blocks replicating the late-18th century Derge Edition. The blocks are faithful replicas of the originals, with no additions, deletions, or significant edits. BDRC's scans of the original Derge edition often contain unclear passages due to woodblock wear. This new print provides a clearer reference in such instances.\n\nChakung Jigme Wangdrak Rinpoche, founder of the Abhaya Fellowship in California, commissioned the carving and printing of thirteen copies, distributed to major Nyingma monasteries in Tibet and beyond. Pema Taré served as the project's patron, without whom it would not have been possible." ,
      "lang" : "en"
    }
